Chef's knife with fixed blade, stainless steel, plastic handle: heading 8211 (knives with cutting blades, serrated or not) covers "other knives having fixed blades" in 8211.92. Subheading 8211.92: "Other knives having fixed blades." Under it, statistical suffixes: 8211.92.20 "Other knives with fixed blades: Having handles of rubber or plastics" (I recall 8211.92.20 is "Having rubber or plastic handles"?). Let me recall: 8211.92 Other knives having fixed blades: 8211.92.20 Hunting knives, fishing knives and utility knives, with a blade of 15.24 cm or less?? Actually 8211.92.20 is "Having rubber or plastic handles"? And 8211.92.30 "Other" with handles of wood... Let me recall: 8211.92.20 "Hunting knives, fishing knives and utility knives, with a blade over 15.24 cm"? Hmm.

Actual HTS: 8211.92 Other knives having fixed blades: 8211.92.20 Hunting knives, fishing knives and utility knives; 8211.92.30 Other: Having handles of wood? 8211.92.40 Having handles of rubber or plastics...; 8211.92.60 Other, with handles of other materials: 8211.92.60 "Other"; 8211.92.90 Other. Kitchen chef's knives with plastic handles are commonly classified in 8211.92.90 ... I recall CBP rulings for chef's knives with plastic handles: 8211.92.9000? Hmm, older rulings: "8211.92.6000, HTSUS, which provides for other knives having fixed blades: other: having rubber or plastic handles"? I think 8211.92.60 is "Other: with rubber or plastics handles" — rulings for kitchen knives with plastic handles cite 8211.92.9000? I'll go with 8211.92.6000 ... Actually I recall 8211.92.90 "Other: Other" stat 8211.92.9000 and 8211.92.60 "Other: Having rubber or plastics handles"? Choose 8211.92.60.60 isn't sure. I'll answer 8211.92.9000? Ruling memory: "The applicable subheading for the chef's knife with a plastic handle will be 8211.92.9000"? I think the 2020s rulings with Delrin handle say 8211.92.9000... go.

